                        "username": "nasamuffin"
                    },
                    "message": "It looks like this was the preexisting verbiage, but \"regular\" doesn't mean very much to me. Is it clearer to say \"persistent\" and \"one-time\" rather than \"regular\" and \"one-time\"?\n\nWhile you're changing the subject, please also prepend \"settings:\" to indicate which component the change will touch."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 15,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Emily Shaffer",
                        "email": "emilyshaffer@google.com",
                        "username": "nasamuffin"
                    },
                    "message": "Please add a Tested: line."
                },
                {
                    "file": "settings.cpp",
                    "line": 98,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Emily Shaffer",
                        "email": "emilyshaffer@google.com",
                        "username": "nasamuffin"
                    },
                    "message": "I'm thinking. Maybe this sounds better as \"ambiguousOperationCount\" - as having more than one interface object means there is some question of which types of set are supported?\n\nI don't think this matters very much, but I'm trying to futureproof against the idea of some third setting type (I don't know, maybe \"factory reset default\"???) presenting itself that we want to support. Since we expect no more updates to the IPMI spec, it probably doesn't matter and is fine the way it is."
                },
                {
                    "file": "settings.cpp",
                    "line": 107,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Emily Shaffer",
                        "email": "emilyshaffer@google.com",
                        "username": "nasamuffin"
                    },
                    "message": "nit: s/is/are/ to agree with plural \"objects\""
                },
                {
                    "file": "settings.cpp",
                    "line": 120,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Emily Shaffer",
                        "email": "emilyshaffer@google.com",
                        "username": "nasamuffin"
                    },
                    "message": "Hmm. I think that this logic would also \"just work\" if for some reason we had a setting that exposed only the one-time object, and not the persistent object. So maybe it makes sense to generalize the comment here to say something more like \"If there's just one object, that's the only kind of setting mode this interface supports, so just return that setting path.\""
                },
                {
                    "file": "settings.cpp",
                    "line": 133,
                    "reviewer": {
